Z||000000||RoadRocket||07-22-2001||01:15 PM||||What's the name for the "plastic stuff" that is part of the Fiero's interior infrastructure. The pieces that support my A/C and Radio, as well as, my transaxle are broken, I need to replace them and am not sure what to call them.<P>Also, any good ideas as to where I can find a replacement? Other than the junk yard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-22-2001||01:20 PM||||For the plastic parts give Pondski a shout, he might have them.  As far as the transaxle I am not sure.  Why don't you post on the forum mall and see if anyone has one?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||07-22-2001||04:26 PM||||They are called fascias. The radio pod fascia, and the shifter fascia. Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RoadRocket||07-22-2001||05:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B>They are called fascias. The radio pod fascia, and the shifter fascia. Hope this helps   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope. Not the fascias, but rather the stuff that the fascias bolt on to. That is what is broken.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-22-2001||05:54 PM||||Could you be referring to the center console support?  Black, sorta webbed thing that runs from just under the ECM up under the stereo and up to the vents.  Best of luck finding a "perfect" one without cracks and broken screw holes.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||RoadRocket||07-23-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Could you be referring to the center console support?  Black, sorta webbed thing that runs from just under the ECM up under the stereo and up to the vents.  Best of luck finding a "perfect" one without cracks and broken screw holes.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That be it.<P>And I was afraid that that would be the answer.<P>No one has the molds an is making new ones? Preferable metal this time?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-24-2001||06:40 PM||||I think it would take a lot of work to make that out of metal.  Probably be very cost prohibitive.  I searched everywhere before I finally found mine.  It's not perfect, but pretty close.  A couple screw holes are stripped and it has developed a couple small cracks but it's much better than the last 3 or 4 I've had.  I don't know how difficult it would be to make out of fiberglass.  I wouldn't mind a "new" one out of a sturdier material for a reasonable price.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||RoadRocket||07-25-2001||12:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>I don't know how difficult it would be to make out of fiberglass.  I wouldn't mind a "new" one out of a sturdier material for a reasonable price.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll just settle for one that lasts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
